{"name":"Pavement","hex":"#554f53","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pavement","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A paved surface; a hard covering on the ground. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A paved path, for the use of pedestrians, located at the side of a road."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pavement"}],"entries":[{"title":"Road surface","blocks":[{"text":"A road surface or pavement is the durable surface material laid down on an area intended to sustain vehicular or foot traffic, such as a road or walkway. In the past, gravel road surfaces, macadam, hoggin, cobblestone and sett granite were extensively used, but these have mostly been replaced by asphalt or concrete laid on a compacted base course. Asphalt mixtures have been used in pavement construction since the beginning of the 20th century and are of two types: metalled (hard-surfaced) and unmetalled roads. Metalled roadways are made to sustain vehicular load and so are usually made on frequently used roads. Unmetalled roads, also known as gravel roads or dirt roads, are rough and can sustain less weight. Road surfaces are frequently marked to guide traffic."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Road_resurfacing.jpg/330px-Road_resurfacing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Road_surface","wikidata":"Q1049667"},{"title":"Sidewalk","blocks":[{"text":"A sidewalk, pavement or footpath is a footpath along the side of a road or street, designed primarily for pedestrians and low-speed personal transporters such as mobility scooters and postal NEVs. Sidewalks are usually paved by concrete, pavers, bricks, tiles, stones or asphalt, and are normally slightly elevated from the roadway and separated from motor vehicle lanes by a curb or gutter. There may also be a planted strip between the sidewalk and the roadway and between the roadway and the adjacent buildings, land lots and private properties."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Pompei_-_panoramio_%2826%29.jpg/330px-Pompei_-_panoramio_%2826%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sidewalk","wikidata":"Q177749"},{"title":"Pavement (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Pavement is an American indie rock band that formed in Stockton, California in 1989. For most of their career, the group consisted of vocalist and guitarist Stephen Malkmus, guitarist and vocalist Scott Kannberg, bassist Mark Ibold, drummer Steve West and vocalist and multi-instrumentalist Bob Nastanovich. Initially conceived as a recording project, the band at first avoided press or live performances, while attracting considerable underground attention with their early releases. Gradually evolving into a more polished band, Pavement recorded five full-length albums and ten EPs over the course of a decade, though the group disbanded with some acrimony in 1999 as the members moved on to other projects. In 2010, Pavement undertook a well-received reunion tour, followed by another international tour from 2022 to 2024. The band has played several smaller tours and concerts since then."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Pavement%2C_the_band%2C_in_Tokyo.jpg/330px-Pavement%2C_the_band%2C_in_Tokyo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pavement_(band)","wikidata":"Q922445"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/2004feb20_Aanleg_rood_fietspad.jpg/500px-2004feb20_Aanleg_rood_fietspad.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/2004feb20_Aanleg_rood_fietspad.jpg/1280px-2004feb20_Aanleg_rood_fietspad.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/2004feb20_Aanleg_rood_fietspad.jpg/500px-2004feb20_Aanleg_rood_fietspad.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Red surfacing for a bicycle lane in the Netherlands","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A2004feb20_Aanleg_rood_fietspad.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Stealth_Communications_laying_down_asphalt_over_fiber-optic_trench_in_NYC.jpg/500px-Stealth_Communications_laying_down_asphalt_over_fiber-optic_trench_in_NYC.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Stealth_Communications_laying_down_asphalt_over_fiber-optic_trench_in_NYC.jpg/1280px-Stealth_Communications_laying_down_asphalt_over_fiber-optic_trench_in_NYC.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Stealth_Communications_laying_down_asphalt_over_fiber-optic_trench_in_NYC.jpg/500px-Stealth_Communications_laying_down_asphalt_over_fiber-optic_trench_in_NYC.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Construction crew laying down asphalt over fiber-optic trench, in New York City","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStealth_Communications_laying_down_asphalt_over_fiber-optic_trench_in_NYC.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Carved_steps_along_Ancient_Roman_Road.jpg/500px-Carved_steps_along_Ancient_Roman_Road.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Carved_steps_along_Ancient_Roman_Road.jpg/1280px-Carved_steps_along_Ancient_Roman_Road.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Carved_steps_along_A